D-Link AQUILA PRO AI M30/M60 A1: MAC aus Odm per Layout-Parser statt fester Zelle

Device Tree M30 und M60: nvmem-layout "dlink,odm-layout" statt
fixed-layout mit macaddr@81 (reg <0x81 0x6>). Kernel-Konfiguration filogic:
den Parser (CONFIG_NVMEM_LAYOUT_DLINK_ODM) fest einbauen; mt7622, mt7623,
mt7629: ausdruecklich abwaehlen, sonst fragt kconfig dort nach dem neuen
Symbol und der Bau bricht ab (der Kernel-Patch gilt fuer alle
mediatek-Subtargets, NVMEM_LAYOUTS ist dort an; zuerst gesehen im Bau
mediatek-mt7622 am 04.10.2026). M30: phy1 bekam
seine MAC per Hotplug fest aus Odm 0x81 (Basis +3); jetzt phy0 (Basis +2,
aus dem Parser) plus 1, gleicher Wert ohne festen Offset. Der Parser selbst
kommt als Kernel-Patch 451-nvmem-add-layout-for-D-Link-Odm.patch.

Hintergrund: Geraete aus Mehrfach-Packs tragen die Kennung "M60-2" bzw.
"M30/CP" statt "M60"/"M30", der MAC-Eintrag rutscht dadurch (M60-2: 0x83,
M30/CP: 0x87). OpenWrt PR 23902 (fester Offset 0x83, geschlossen) und
PR 24967 (Suche per Shell-Skript, offen).

diff -ru a/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7981b-dlink-aquila-pro-ai-m30-a1.dts b/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7981b-dlink-aquila-pro-ai-m30-a1.dts
--- a/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7981b-dlink-aquila-pro-ai-m30-a1.dts
+++ b/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7981b-dlink-aquila-pro-ai-m30-a1.dts
@@ -205,13 +205,9 @@
 				read-only;
 
 				nvmem-layout {
-					compatible = "fixed-layout";
-					#address-cells = <1>;
-					#size-cells = <1>;
+					compatible = "dlink,odm-layout";
 
-					macaddr_odm: macaddr@81 {
-						compatible = "mac-base";
-						reg = <0x81 0x6>;
+					macaddr_odm: macaddr {
 						#nvmem-cell-cells = <1>;
 					};
 				};
diff -ru a/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7986a-dlink-aquila-pro-ai-m60-a1.dts b/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7986a-dlink-aquila-pro-ai-m60-a1.dts
--- a/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7986a-dlink-aquila-pro-ai-m60-a1.dts
+++ b/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7986a-dlink-aquila-pro-ai-m60-a1.dts
@@ -276,13 +276,9 @@
 				read-only;
 
 				nvmem-layout {
-					compatible = "fixed-layout";
-					#address-cells = <1>;
-					#size-cells = <1>;
+					compatible = "dlink,odm-layout";
 
-					macaddr_odm: macaddr@81 {
-						compatible = "mac-base";
-						reg = <0x81 0x6>;
+					macaddr_odm: macaddr {
 						#nvmem-cell-cells = <1>;
 					};
 				};
diff -ru a/target/linux/mediatek/filogic/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/11_fix_wifi_mac b/target/linux/mediatek/filogic/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/11_fix_wifi_mac
--- a/target/linux/mediatek/filogic/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/11_fix_wifi_mac
+++ b/target/linux/mediatek/filogic/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/11_fix_wifi_mac
@@ -95,8 +95,11 @@
 		[ "$PHYNBR" = "1" ] && macaddr_setbit_la $(macaddr_add $addr 1) > /sys${DEVPATH}/macaddress
 		;;
 	dlink,aquila-pro-ai-m30-a1)
-		addr=$(mtd_get_mac_binary "Odm" 0x81)
-		[ "$PHYNBR" = "1" ] && macaddr_add $addr 3 > /sys${DEVPATH}/macaddress
+		# phy0 gets base+2 from the dlink,odm-layout cell; the MAC record in
+		# Odm has no fixed offset (multi-pack units), so derive phy1 (base+3)
+		# from phy0 instead of reading Odm 0x81.
+		addr=$(cat /sys/class/ieee80211/phy0/macaddress)
+		[ "$PHYNBR" = "1" ] && macaddr_add $addr 1 > /sys${DEVPATH}/macaddress
 		;;
 	glinet,gl-mt6000|\
 	glinet,gl-x3000|\
